                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 537.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Langston to Mr. Damier.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-03-31"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 31,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The undersigned has the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your dispatch dated March 29, 1883, having reference
                    to the condition of affairs at Miragoâne, and to tender you his thanks
                    therefor.</p>
                <p>With sentiments, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN MERCER LANGSTON.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
